            <ArticleTitle>[Pain therapy other than with drugs with special reference to headache].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>600-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain-control and pain-therapy becomes most efficient within a systematic polypragmasy combining pharmacological and non-pharmacological means. the non-pharmacological means as well have to be combined in a rational (not casual) way. Plurality of methods should be controlled by a holistic medical view, not to become monomaniac. On the other hand specialized development in methods must be stimulated. Within our own working group we have developed a special model of group therapy combining autogenic training and analytical approach. We also apply respiratory feedback combined with suggestive formula implanted into the hypnoid state.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
